  "body": "While the [specification note](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/nav-history-apis.html#shared-history-push/replace-state-steps:~:text=Note%20how%20only%20the%20URL%20of%20the%20Document%20matters%2C%20and%20not%20its%20origin.%20They%20can%20mismatch%20in%20cases%20like%20about%3Ablank%20Documents%20with%20inherited%20origins%2C%20in%20sandboxed%20iframes%2C%20or%20when%20the%20document.domain%20setter%20has%20been%20used.) around only checking URL in push/replace state makes sense for defending attacks from documents which modified document.domain, this doesn't make sense for CSP sandbox because it is likely to host untrustworthy content which can spoof URL using History API.\r\n\r\n## Repro steps\r\n1. Go to  https://test.shhnjk.com/csp_sandbox.php?s=allow-scripts&xss=%3Cform%3E%3Ch2%3EPassword%20Please%3C/h2%3E%3Cinput%20type=text%3E%3Cinput%20type=password%3E%3Cbutton%3Elogin%3C/button%3E%3C/form%3E%3Cscript%3Ehistory.pushState(%27%27,%27%27,%27/login%27)%3C/script%3E on Firefox.\r\n2. Observe that the URL changes to https://test.shhnjk.com/login.",
